-- title:
--   Uniqueness of place specialisations when the special fibre has positive genus
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $N \ge 1$, and $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ equipped with a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} \colon A \to k$. Let `data` consist of a monic $\Phi \in (\mathbb{Z}[X])[Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ with $\Phi$ evaluated at the $j$-substitution and $j_q$ equal to zero, and let `hKr` assert the Kronecker congruence, i.e. that the bivariate reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $q$ equals $(C(X)^q - X)\,(C(X) - X^q)$. Let `hα`, `hβ` assert that the two Hecke maps `heckeAlphaBar`, `heckeBetaBar` from the base change of the full modular function field of level $N$ to that of level $Nq$, over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, are integral ring homomorphisms. Assume $q \nmid N$ and that the genus $\dim_k H^1(0)$ of the field $k(\bar j, \bar j_N) \subseteq k((q))$, generated by the two $q$-expansion coordinates, is positive. Then any two elements $P$, $P'$ of `PlaceSpecialization A q N data hKr k red hα hβ` — packets consisting of a map from places of the level-$N$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to places over $k$, a homomorphism from $J_0$ to the degree-zero divisor class group over $k$, and compatibility axioms comparing orders of $\bar j$, $\bar j_N$ and their translates by elements of $A$ through $\mathrm{red}$ — coincide: $P = P'$.
--
--   The assertion is that the type of specialisation packets for the level-$N$ modular curve at a prime $q$ of good reduction is a subsingleton, so that the reduction map on places and the induced map on degree-zero divisor classes are uniquely determined by the coordinate clauses once the special fibre has positive genus. It is used alongside the corresponding existence statement, which produces a prolongation tuple satisfying the model, regularity and node-value laws.
